The verdict is FINDINGS, not PASS: audio correctness is still unverified, because nobody has listened to it. The report is at `artifacts/logs/reviewer_gameplay.6zun55/report.md`.

I tested the existing `dist/` build in headless Chromium without rebuilding it. The source diff has changed since the last review, but the `.wasm` hash is the same.

- **Movement:** all of this passed.
  - Forward hold, then release, coasts and stops with normal Doom momentum.
  - Strafe and Shift-run move the view.
  - Focus loss stops an in-progress turn.
- **Play:** the tic rate is 35.0/s, including after returning to the page. Fire changes ammo and plays SFX, and held fire repeats. The Esc menu freezes the view. There were no page errors.
- **Audio:** the audio context starts suspended and is running after a key press. Level music switches, and the audio clock advanced 2.005 s per 2.003 s of wall time. There were 11 SFX played, 0 bad SFX, 0 music errors and a peak of 0.43. That shows sound is being produced, not that it sounds right.
- **One FAIL in my script:** the check "menu SFX and music heard" failed. I think it expects an effect too early, because no sound effect is due right after the first Enter on the title screen. I didn't confirm that, so I listed it as a script problem to fix or drop.

Still unverified:
- **Audio by ear:** needs a human on a headed machine.
- **Real hidden-tab behaviour:** headless can't produce a hidden tab.
- **Not covered at all:** walking through a door, level exit, pickups, damage and death, Firefox, Safari and HiDPI.

The report also lists the owners and my assumptions. WASD and mouse are not mapped, and the music is an oscillator synth rather than the Doom instrument set.

The only thing I started was the local web server, and I stopped it.